  {
   "k": "hav5b2",
   "en": "If you did not get ⟦0⟧ in the peace deal or did not get a peace deal with the ⟦1⟧ before the ⟦2⟧ joined, it is going to take you a while. You have several options after building up your army: Defeat the Axis (wait until they progressed quite a bit into the Soviet Union) - >Take Canada in the peace deal -> Justify on Mexico - > Defeat the USA - > Defeat Mexico. Justify on China -> Declare war -> Leave the Axis and join Japan in the Greater East-Asian Co-Prosperity Sphere - > Defeat China together -> Defeat USA together -> Annex the American border with Mexico -> Justify on Mexico. Depending on the how much of the British Fleet you took or how much of your own Navy you had to build in order to take the UK, you can also try naval invasions. If you try from Greenland, it is such a short distance from Canada that you can usually get the required Naval Dominance to launch an invasion across that single sea zone before the enemy fleets arrive. If you lost Greenland, you can island hop from the Faroe Islands to Iceland to Greenland to Canada as well using the same strategy. If El Salvador is in the Axis and still alive, you can also just naval invade, paradrop, or even justify a war goal through Guatemala (though this is actually tricky because the war ends so fast you literally might not be able to walk through the country to get to Mexican land in time).",
